can turn to rust
If he could only find
that feeling once again
If we could only change
the way the story ends

And he may still come home
But I live here alone
The love that built these walls
is gone

Home ...

Home ain't where his heart is anymore
He may hang his hat
behind our bedroom door
But he don't lay his head down
to love me like before

Home ...

He don't lay his head down
to love me like before
Home ain't where his heart is anymore

No, Home ain't where his heart is
